{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7d7BWLWVNb91v1xbpscw5","type":"tool_result","content":"test('adopt: a tag mismatch warns and leaves that subtree', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<div><span title=\"a\"></span></div>' +\n        '<p title=\"a\"></p>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    const warns:unknown[] = []\n    const warn = console.warn\n    console.warn = (...a:unknown[]) => { warns.push(a) }\n    const title = signal('a')\n    try {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<div><em title=${title}></em></div><p\n            title=${title}></p>`)\n    } finally {\n        console.warn = warn\n    }\n    t.equal(warns.length, 1, 'warned once')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'nothing changed on adoption')\n    title('b')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('span')!.getAttribute('title'), 'a',\n        'mismatched subtree untouched')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('p')!.getAttribute('title'), 'b',\n        'sibling still bound')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\nfunction quietly (fn:() => void):unknown[] {\n    const warns:unknown[] = []\n    const warn = console.warn\n    console.warn = (...a:unknown[]) => { warns.push(a) }\n    try {\n        fn()\n    } finally {\n        console.warn = warn\n    }\n    return warns\n}\n\ntest('adopt: a button after a multi-node raw() is bound', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<div><b>a</b>\\n<i>b</i><button>go</button></div>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    let clicks = 0\n    const warns = quietly(() => {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<div>${braw('<b>a</b>\\n<i>b</i>')}<button\n            onclick=${() => { clicks++ }}>go</button></div>`)\n    })\n    t.equal(warns.length, 0, 'no adoption warning')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'adoption changed nothing')\n    box.querySelector('button')!.click()\n    t.equal(clicks, 1, 'listener is attached')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\ntest('adopt: a bound attribute after text-and-element raw() updates', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<p>hi <b>a</b> <i>c</i>' +\n        '<span title=\"a\"></span></p>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    const title = signal('a')\n    const warns = quietly(() => {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<p>${braw('hi <b>a</b> <i>c</i>')}<span\n            title=${title}></span></p>`)\n    })\n    t.equal(warns.length, 0, 'no adoption warning')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'adoption changed nothing')\n    title('b')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('span')!.getAttribute('title'), 'b',\n        'attribute is bound')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\n// Attribute mutations under `root` caused by `fn`.\nfunction attrWrites (root:Node, fn:() => void):MutationRecord[] {\n    const obs = new MutationObserver(() => {})\n    obs.observe(root, { attributes: true, subtree: true })\n    try {\n        fn()\n        return obs.takeRecords()\n    } finally {\n        obs.disconnect()\n    }\n}\n\nbrowser finds that range by its `<!--[c-->` marker, skipping nested\nhosts, and matches its close by nesting depth, so a region in the\nhost's own render is never mistaken for the children.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n\nValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\nstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\nthe affected region.\n\nChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\nchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbb096a4-5a11-460d-8a94-f641e7ace0de","uuid":"9b6928fb-23ce-475c-a0c1-4e8956a17c74","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:24:05.609Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"test('adopt: a tag mismatch warns and leaves that subtree', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<div><span title=\"a\"></span></div>' +\n        '<p title=\"a\"></p>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    const warns:unknown[] = []\n    const warn = console.warn\n    console.warn = (...a:unknown[]) => { warns.push(a) }\n    const title = signal('a')\n    try {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<div><em title=${title}></em></div><p\n            title=${title}></p>`)\n    } finally {\n        console.warn = warn\n    }\n    t.equal(warns.length, 1, 'warned once')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'nothing changed on adoption')\n    title('b')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('span')!.getAttribute('title'), 'a',\n        'mismatched subtree untouched')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('p')!.getAttribute('title'), 'b',\n        'sibling still bound')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\nfunction quietly (fn:() => void):unknown[] {\n    const warns:unknown[] = []\n    const warn = console.warn\n    console.warn = (...a:unknown[]) => { warns.push(a) }\n    try {\n        fn()\n    } finally {\n        console.warn = warn\n    }\n    return warns\n}\n\ntest('adopt: a button after a multi-node raw() is bound', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<div><b>a</b>\\n<i>b</i><button>go</button></div>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    let clicks = 0\n    const warns = quietly(() => {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<div>${braw('<b>a</b>\\n<i>b</i>')}<button\n            onclick=${() => { clicks++ }}>go</button></div>`)\n    })\n    t.equal(warns.length, 0, 'no adoption warning')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'adoption changed nothing')\n    box.querySelector('button')!.click()\n    t.equal(clicks, 1, 'listener is attached')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\ntest('adopt: a bound attribute after text-and-element raw() updates', t => {\n    const box = adoptBox('<p>hi <b>a</b> <i>c</i>' +\n        '<span title=\"a\"></span></p>')\n    const before = box.innerHTML\n    const title = signal('a')\n    const warns = quietly(() => {\n        mount(box, bhtml`<p>${braw('hi <b>a</b> <i>c</i>')}<span\n            title=${title}></span></p>`)\n    })\n    t.equal(warns.length, 0, 'no adoption warning')\n    t.equal(box.innerHTML, before, 'adoption changed nothing')\n    title('b')\n    t.equal(box.querySelector('span')!.getAttribute('title'), 'b',\n        'attribute is bound')\n    box.remove()\n})\n\n// Attribute mutations under `root` caused by `fn`.\nfunction attrWrites (root:Node, fn:() => void):MutationRecord[] {\n    const obs = new MutationObserver(() => {})\n    obs.observe(root, { attributes: true, subtree: true })\n    try {\n        fn()\n        return obs.takeRecords()\n    } finally {\n        obs.disconnect()\n    }\n}\n\nbrowser finds that range by its `<!--[c-->` marker, skipping nested\nhosts, and matches its close by nesting depth, so a region in the\nhost's own render is never mistaken for the children.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop