{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PVh6SxvQo4XCLbwGhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Server DOM `<h1><p><button>` adopted against markup `<p><button>` logs one warning at most and the button's listener fires\n[x] Server DOM `<p><button>` adopted against markup `<h1><p><button>` logs one warning and the button's listener fires\n[x] The skipped server nodes are the same node objects after adoption\n[x] `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\nTicket 06 is finished and committed. One extra or missing server node now costs one warning, and the siblings after it stay bound. `npm test` passes 421/421, lint is clean and `npm run size` passes, but only because I raised the browser templater's size limit.\n\n**The fix** is in the mismatch branch of `_adopt` in `src/htm.browser.ts`:\n1. A tag mismatch always calls `console.warn`.\n2. Adoption then searches the later siblings in the same range for the first element with the expected tag. It steps over whole `<!--[-->` and `<!--[c-->` ranges, so it never adopts an element from inside a region. If it finds one, it adopts it and leaves the skipped server nodes in place.\n3. If it finds none, the DOM cursor stays put, so the next markup item is tried against the same node.\n\nThe warning fires even when the search finds the element, which fits the ticket's \"one warning at most\".\n\n**Tests:** I added two adoption tests in `test/index.ts`, one with an extra `<h1>` on the server and one with an extra `<h1>` in the markup. Each checks the warning count, that the HTML is unchanged, that the server node is the same object, and that the button's listener fires. Both failed before the fix and pass after it. The existing mismatch test still passes.\n\n**Size:** the browser templater went from under its 4.95 kB limit to 4.99 kB. As the ticket allows, I raised the limit in `.size-limit.js` to 5 kB and recorded it in an ADR-007 note.\n\n**Docs:** ADR-007 now says the mismatch warning is always on and describes the search. I also updated the line in AGENTS.md that still said a mismatch skips one node. My notes for this ticket are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":361,"cache_read_input_tokens":69759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":361},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbb096a4-5a11-460d-8a94-f641e7ace0de","uuid":"442bfb20-434f-48e2-8d2c-0c8dbfe91b37","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:26:09.974Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3PVgp6G8b1dTcQvPS4m"}
